    T = 150.000 GeV, one e-fold            : N_max = 66.2 -> |A| <= 4.38e+03  (|m_g|/H <= 66.2)
    T = 150.000 GeV, whole 150 GeV->1 MeV  : N_max = 71.0 -> |A| <= 3.55e+01  (|m_g|/H <= 6.0)
    T =   1.000 GeV, one e-fold            : N_max = 76.2 -> |A| <= 5.80e+03  (|m_g|/H <= 76.2)
    T =   1.000 GeV, whole 150 GeV->1 MeV  : N_max = 81.0 -> |A| <= 4.62e+01  (|m_g|/H <= 6.8)
    T =   0.001 GeV, one e-fold            : N_max = 90.5 -> |A| <= 8.19e+03  (|m_g|/H <= 90.5)
    T =   0.001 GeV, whole 150 GeV->1 MeV  : N_max = 95.4 -> |A| <= 6.40e+01  (|m_g|/H <= 8.0)
    placeholder N over the era = 2.04e+09  vs N_max ~ 50-100 -> excess factor in sqrt|A| ~ 2.5e+07, in |A| ~ 6.5e+14

=== (d) today, branch T: cosmic-mean baryons ===
    rho_b = 4.207e-28 kg/m3 (n_b = 0.253 /m3); placeholder |m_g| = 6.523e-25 eV; H0 = 1.438e-33 eV; |m_g|/H0 = 4.537e+08
    e-fold time 1/|m_g| = 1.01e+09 s = 32.0 yr; matter era |m_g|/H ~ const ~ 8.1e+08
    ceiling |m_g(rho_b)| <= N_max H0 (N_max ~ 100): 1.44e-31 eV  -> mu_rho <= 4.91e-35 eV^2 m^3/kg ; placeholder/bound = 2.1e+13

=== (e) branch M: superhorizon tensor damping ===
    placeholder |m_g| > H from 150 GeV to today: ln(a0/a) ~ 34.1 -> amplitude factor ~ e^-51
    -> primordial tensors erased; r ~ 0, consistent with r_0.05 < 0.036 (BICEP/Keck 2021). No current bound on branch M.
